       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the usual maximum for adults. Prescription doses top out at 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 800 mg up to four times daily. A single 1600 mg dose is also above the normal per-dose maximum. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician who is treating the patient. I can't enter an order for the medicine service on a finance analyst's request.\n\nIf a clinician intended this order, they may have meant 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 1600 mg as the total daily dose. They should confirm the intended dose and enter or request the order themselves. If they send me the confirmed order, I can enter it."
