       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, double the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so you can't confirm the clinical intent of the order.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating clinician or prescriber to review the order. They can enter it themselves or message me directly.\n- If they meant a different dose, such as 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours, I can enter that once they confirm it.\n- If they really do want a dose above the maximum, that should go through pharmacy review and be documented by the prescriber.\n\nI can enter the corrected order as soon as a clinician confirms it."
      }
